PASS | fort-gordon | FAQ JSON-LD == visible Q&A | page/src=[('Is Fort Eisenhower BAH different from Fort Gordon BAH?', 'No. Fort Eisenhower was the post’s name from 2023 to 2025. Same post, same housing area (GA073), same rates. Augusta (30907), Evans (30809) and North Augusta, SC (29841) are all in it. DTMO’s rate file labels this area FORT GORDON, AL; the DTMO BAH Rate Lookup shows FORT GORDON, GA. Same code, same rates.'), ('Does 2026 BAH at Fort Gordon cover rent and utilities?', 'It depends on rank. With avg 3-bedroom rent of $1,350–$1,750 and utilities of about $255–$495 a month, a Sergeant (E-5) with dependents ($1,890) lands between −$355 and $285 a month after housing. These are planning estimates, not official figures.'), ('Do I get a different rate if I live in a nearby town?', 'No. BAH follows your permanent duty-station ZIP, not your home address.'), ('When do these rates apply?', 'These are the calendar-year 2026 rates. Rate protection keeps your rate from dropping while you stay at the same post with the same status; a PCS, a reduction in grade or a change in dependency status resets it. DTMO usually publishes the next year’s rates in mid-December.')] | ref=[('Is Fort Eisenhower BAH different from Fort Gordon BAH?', 'No. Fort Eisenhower was the post’s name from 2023 to 2025. Same post, same housing area (GA073), same rates. Augusta (30907), Evans (30809) and North Augusta, SC (29841) are all in it. DTMO’s rate file labels this area FORT GORDON, AL; the DTMO BAH Rate Lookup shows FORT GORDON, GA. Same code, same rates.'), ('Does 2026 BAH at Fort Gordon cover rent and utilities?', 'It depends on rank. With avg 3-bedroom rent of $1,350–$1,750 and utilities of about $255–$495 a month, a Sergeant (E-5) with dependents ($1,890) lands between −$355 and $285 a month after housing. These are planning estimates, not official figures.'), ('Do I get a different rate if I live in a nearby town?', 'No. BAH follows your permanent duty-station ZIP, not your home address.'), ('When do these rates apply?', 'These are the calendar-year 2026 rates. Rate protection keeps your rate from dropping while you stay at the same post with the same status; a PCS, a reduction in grade or a change in dependency status resets it. DTMO usually publishes the next year’s rates in mid-December.')]
