PASS | fort-jackson | FAQ JSON-LD == visible Q&A | page/src=[('Why does DTMO call it Columbia/Fort Jackson?', 'DTMO sets BAH by Military Housing Area, and Fort Jackson shares one area with the city of Columbia: COLUMBIA/FORT JACKSON, SC (SC260). Northeast Columbia ZIPs such as 29229 and 29223 use the same rates.'), ('Does 2026 BAH at Fort Jackson cover rent and utilities?', 'It depends on rank. With avg 3-bedroom rent of $1,350–$1,850 and utilities of about $255–$505 a month, a Sergeant (E-5) with dependents ($1,878) lands between −$477 and $273 a month after housing. These are planning estimates, not official figures.'), ('Do I get a different rate if I live in a nearby town?', 'No. BAH follows your permanent duty-station ZIP, not your home address.'), ('When do these rates apply?', 'These are the calendar-year 2026 rates. Rate protection keeps your rate from dropping while you stay at the same post with the same status; a PCS, a reduction in grade or a change in dependency status resets it. DTMO usually publishes the next year’s rates in mid-December.')] | ref=[('Why does DTMO call it Columbia/Fort Jackson?', 'DTMO sets BAH by Military Housing Area, and Fort Jackson shares one area with the city of Columbia: COLUMBIA/FORT JACKSON, SC (SC260). Northeast Columbia ZIPs such as 29229 and 29223 use the same rates.'), ('Does 2026 BAH at Fort Jackson cover rent and utilities?', 'It depends on rank. With avg 3-bedroom rent of $1,350–$1,850 and utilities of about $255–$505 a month, a Sergeant (E-5) with dependents ($1,878) lands between −$477 and $273 a month after housing. These are planning estimates, not official figures.'), ('Do I get a different rate if I live in a nearby town?', 'No. BAH follows your permanent duty-station ZIP, not your home address.'), ('When do these rates apply?', 'These are the calendar-year 2026 rates. Rate protection keeps your rate from dropping while you stay at the same post with the same status; a PCS, a reduction in grade or a change in dependency status resets it. DTMO usually publishes the next year’s rates in mid-December.')]
